-- title:
--   Rationality of a closed-fibre section gives a closed point
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $O$ be a commutative local ring, with residue field $\kappa = O/\mathfrak m$ obtained as `IsLocalRing.ResidueField O`. Write $\mathfrak X$ for `DRModel p`, the two-chart integral model over $\mathbb Z$ attached to the function field `modularFunctionFieldFull p` (the intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \mathbb Q((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions at level $p$) and to the element `IgusaScheme.jFull p` of that field, i.e. the pushout of the two affine charts, together with the structure morphism `DRModel.toBase p :` $\mathfrak X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ obtained from the algebra maps $\mathbb Z \to$ `chartAlgFin`, `chartAlgInf`. Suppose given a morphism of schemes $s \colon \operatorname{Spec}\kappa \to \mathfrak X \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z} \operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ which is a section of the second projection, i.e. $s$ followed by `pullback.snd` is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$. Let $x$ be the image of $s$ evaluated at the unique (closed) point of $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ under the map on underlying topological spaces of `DRModel.baseChangeMap (IsLocalRing.residue O)`, the morphism $\mathfrak X \times_{\mathbb Z} \operatorname{Spec}\kappa \to \mathfrak X \times_{\mathbb Z} \operatorname{Spec} O$ given by the identity on $\mathfrak X$ and by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map $O \to \kappa$. The assertion is that $\{x\}$ is a closed subset of the underlying space of $\mathfrak X \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z} \operatorname{Spec} O$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a $\kappa$-rational point of the closed fibre of the integral model is a closed point of the model over $O$, used when the crossing points of the fibre at $p$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model are assumed rational over the residue field. It is cited in the construction of the resolved model package, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts).
